# Recordings, decoded events, the SQLite store, logs, the worker token.
# Everything a running station produces. None of it belongs in git, and some of
# it is other people's radio traffic.
var/

# YOUR station's configuration: coordinates, band plan, watchlist, claimed
# sensors, notifier credentials. The worked examples in config/examples/ ARE
# tracked; anything you copy out of them is not.
#
# This is the line that keeps a public checkout publishable. Point
# BANDWATCH_CONFIG at a directory outside the repo if you would rather not rely
# on it.
config/*
!config/examples/
!config/README.md

# Generated from config/lanes.json and config/bandplan.json. Outputs, never
# sources -- hand-edit one and the next generator run silently reverts you.
config/conf/
config/profiles/

# Third-party decoders and datasets: large, re-downloadable, not ours.
# The build notes ARE ours and do ship.
tools/*
!tools/README.md
models/
enrich/data/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.venv-test/
.DS_Store
